    "updated_at": "2024-01-12T22:17:31Z",
    "body": "@jeremyroman There's somewhat a related bug when creating a [pattern parser](https://urlpattern.spec.whatwg.org/#pattern-parser) with some of the [encoding callbacks](https://urlpattern.spec.whatwg.org/#canon-encoding-callbacks).\r\n\r\nThese callbacks also rely on URL spec's basic parser and do not check for `null` value with the exception of the [port canonicalizing callback](https://urlpattern.spec.whatwg.org/#canonicalize-a-port) but as with the base URL the integer port should also be serialized or it fail the first *[escape a regexp string](https://urlpattern.spec.whatwg.org/#escape-a-regexp-string)* assertion.\r\n\r\nAs I understand these callbacks should always return a string, as all patterns are string.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
