    "updated_at": "2024-02-11T14:29:15Z",
    "body": "Hi @jeremyroman, hostnames seems to suffer from the same issue. The basic URL parser will parse a host as a hostname or an [IP address](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#ip-address). Addresses can be represented as an [single integer](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-ipv4) or as an [array of integer](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-ipv6), so they also need to be explicitly serialized, here :\r\n\r\n> To [canonicalize a hostname](https://urlpattern.spec.whatwg.org/#canonicalize-a-hostname) given a string value\r\n> - 5\\. Return dummyURL’s [host](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-host).\r\n\r\nThe parsed host and port in the match steps will also need to be properly serialized :\r\n\r\n> To perform a [match](https://urlpattern.spec.whatwg.org/#urlpattern-match) given a [URLPattern](https://urlpattern.spec.whatwg.org/#urlpattern) urlpattern, a [URLPatternInput](https://urlpattern.spec.whatwg.org/#typedefdef-urlpatterninput) input, and an optional string baseURLString:\r\n> - 12\\. Otherwise:\r\n>   - 8\\. Set hostname to url’s [host](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-host) or the empty string if the value is null.\r\n>   - 9\\. Set port to url’s [port](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-port) or the empty string if the value is null.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
